      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\), we first need to determine the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\).\n\nWe perform the long division of 1 by 7:\n\n1. \\( 1 \\div 7 = 0.142857142857142857\\ldots \\)\n\nThe long division for dividing 1 by 7 is as follows:\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0.\\overline{142857}\\]\n\nThe repeating block of the decimal is \"142857\", which has a length of 6 digits. \n\nNext, we need to find the position of the 100th digit in the repeating block \"142857\".\n\nThe sequence \"142857\" repeats every 6 digits. Therefore, to find the position of the 100th digit, we need to determine the remainder when 100 is divided by 6.\n\n\\[ 100 \\mod 6 = 4 \\]\n\nThis means that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating block \"142857\".\n\nThe 4th digit is 2.\n\nThus, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).\n\nWe may also want to verify with Python that it is indeed 2 at the 100th position.\n```python\n# Python verification\n# The repeating block of the decimal representation of 1/7\nblock = \"142857\"\n\n# The position of the 100th digit\nposition = 100 % len(block)\n\n# Get the digit at the specified position\ndigit_100th = block[position - 1] if position != 0 else block[-1]\nprint(digit_100th)\n```",
